The corpus check changes two reviewer conclusions: shared social VR does expose an omitted Lem claim, but it does not by itself falsify his full “no-exits” phantomat; and Deep Blue is a legitimate HIT on the exact chess sentence, though it is misplaced in the problem-level block. I’ve also found a major issue both missed in the essay’s “persuasion” reading.
